  "content": {
    "id": "p66-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Find values of $k$ for which the parabola $y=kx^{2}+3kx+9$ is always above the $x$-axis.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$0<k<4$",
      "worked": "The parabola must open upwards and have no $x$-intercepts, so $k>0$ and $\\Delta<0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(3k)^{2}-4(k)(9)\\\\&=9k^{2}-36k\\\\9k^{2}-36k&<0\\\\9k(k-4)&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThe parabola $y=9k^{2}-36k$ opens upwards with intercepts $0$ and $4$. It is below the axis between these intercepts.\n$$0<k<4$$\nThis also satisfies $k>0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 45
  },
